DESCRIPTION:Melissa Haendel's research focuses on utilizing data translati
 on and informatics to weave together healthcare systems\, basic science\,
  and patient insights\, with the goal of driving clinical and societal im
 pact. She spearheads the development of data integration technologies and
  standards\, leading global interdisciplinary teams to create diagnostic 
 applications for rare diseases and establish platforms for translational 
 research. Key initiatives she co-founded include the Monarch Initiative\,
  which unites global knowledge on rare diseases for diagnostics and disco
 very\; and the National Clinical Cohort Collaborative (N3C)\, the largest
  publicly-available harmonized dataset of electronic health records.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260406T184714Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260414T123000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T184714Z
